# InterviewOS

**Practice your interview before the real one.**

InterviewOS is an AI-powered interview practice platform. Describe the job you're targeting — role, experience level, company, company type, interview type, and job description — and optionally attach your resume, GitHub profile, or manual project entries. InterviewOS generates a personalized question set and lets you practice two ways: written practice with AI-scored answers, or a live AI spoken mock interview with real-time follow-up questions. Every session ends in a scored, 6-dimension debrief saved to your history.

## Features

- **Personalized question generation** — questions are tailored to your target role, seniority, company type, and interview type, using your resume, GitHub profile, and manual project entries as context.
- **Written practice mode** — answer at your own pace; every answer is scored with structured feedback (strengths, gaps, improvements).
- **AI spoken mock interview** — a browser-based mic + text-to-speech interviewer conducts a live interview with real-time follow-up questions based on your answers.
- **6-dimension scored debrief** — after every mock session, get a structured breakdown of performance, saved to history for tracking progress over time.
- **Cross-session question variation** — an avoid-list of your last 200 generated questions is enforced server-side so repeat practice sessions don't repeat themselves.
- **Graceful AI fallback** — if the AI provider is unavailable, the app degrades to a deterministic question bank, interviewer, and scorer rather than failing outright.

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Framework | Next.js 16 (App Router, React 19, TypeScript) |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4, hand-rolled UI primitives, Lucide icons |
| Database | PostgreSQL on Neon (serverless), Prisma ORM 6 |
| Auth | Email + password (bcrypt), httpOnly JWT session cookie (`jose`, HS256) |
| AI | OpenRouter, behind a provider abstraction with deterministic fallback |
| Voice | Browser-native Web Speech API (STT + TTS) — no third-party voice API, audio never stored |
| Resume parsing | `pdfjs-dist` (server-side, magic-byte validated) |
| Testing | `node:test` via `tsx --test` — 52 tests |

## Architecture Highlights

- **One app, no CORS.** All AI and DB access happens server-side only, via server actions and route handlers — API keys never reach the client.
- **Provider abstraction.** A single facade (`generateQuestions`, `generateFollowUps`, `evaluateAnswer`, `extractResume`, `driveInterview`, `generateDebrief`) handles retries with backoff and falls back to deterministic logic on failure.
- **Streaming generation.** Question generation streams progress via NDJSON stage events so the UI never sits on a blank loading screen.
- **Ownership scoping everywhere.** Every database query is filtered by the authenticated user, enforced consistently across data-access helpers.
- **Accuracy layer.** A 5-band scoring rubric, low-temperature scoring, one-probe-per-question interviewer pacing, and seniority-based difficulty quotas keep feedback consistent and fair.
- **Practice, not employability claims.** Debriefs are generated only from real transcripts (minimum 2 spoken answers) and are explicitly framed as practice feedback — never a hiring signal.

## Getting Started

```bash
npm install
npm run dev        # http://localhost:3000
```

### Environment variables

| Variable | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | Yes | Neon PostgreSQL connection string |
| `AUTH_SECRET` | Yes | Used to sign session JWTs |
| `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` | Yes | Powers question generation, scoring, and the mock interviewer |
| `OPENROUTER_MODEL` | No | Override the default model |
| `OPENROUTER_CHEAP_MODEL` | No | Cheaper model used for extraction tasks |

See `.env.example` for the full template.

### Useful commands

```bash
npm run build         # production build
npm run lint           # lint
npm test               # run the test suite
npx prisma migrate dev # run DB migrations
npm run db:seed        # seed the database
```

## Project Structure

```
src/
  app/            # Next.js App Router pages + API routes
  components/ui/  # Hand-rolled UI primitives
  lib/
    ai/service.ts # AI provider abstraction + fallback
    data.ts       # Ownership-scoped data access
    mock.ts       # Mock interview session logic
    speech.ts     # Swappable browser speech layer
  proxy.ts        # Edge auth gate (Next.js 16's middleware equivalent)
prisma/
  migrations/     # Database migrations
```

## Routes

| Route | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/` | Landing page |
| `/signup`, `/login` | Auth |
| `/dashboard` | Overview |
| `/interviews` | Session list — progress, delete |
| `/interviews/new` | Setup + streaming question generation |
| `/interviews/[id]` | Written practice workspace |
| `/mock/[id]` | Live spoken mock interview |
| `/history`, `/history/[id]` | Past debriefs |
| `/settings` | Account settings |

